course: dictionary
lesson: 2790
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word dismiss is a good example. «Class dismissed!» means the teacher lets the pupils go. It does not mean the children are being sent away in a cross way.
explain: Dismiss can also mean deciding an idea is not worth thinking about. «She dismissed his plan with a wave of her hand.» Her wave shows she thought the plan was silly, so she did not give it a second thought.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In a classroom, a teacher dismisses the class. In cricket, a bowler dismisses a batter, which means gets them out. In a job, an employer may dismiss a worker, which means removes them from their job. The topic tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Dismiss is a verb: dismiss, dismisses, dismissed, dismissing.
fact: «Dismiss» can mean to send people away or let them leave, as in «class dismissed».
fact: «Dismiss an idea» means deciding it is not worth thinking about.
fact: «Dismissed from his job» means removed from work by an employer.
fact: In cricket, to dismiss a batter means to get them out. In US English, «laid off» means dismissed from work because there is not enough work.
exercise: «Class dismissed!» What does dismiss mean here? | *To let the pupils leave | To sing a song | To shout at the class | To start a spelling test
exercise: «She dismissed the idea out of hand.» What does dismissed suggest? | *Decided it was not worth thinking about | Asked everyone to vote for it | Wrote it down carefully | Loved it at once
exercise: «The bowler dismissed the batter with one ball.» In cricket, dismissed means | Ran off the pitch | *Got the batter out | Gave the batter a prize | Hit the ball very hard
test: «The company dismissed the worker after the mistake.» What does dismissed mean here? | Let the worker sit down | Moved the worker to a new office | Gave the worker a day off | *Removed the worker from the job
test: Which sentence uses dismiss to mean let people leave? | «The cat dismissed the mouse from the garden.» | «The farmer dismissed the idea of a new barn.» | «The river dismissed its banks in the flood.» | *«The bell rang and the head teacher dismissed the school.»
exam: «The judge dismissed the case before it reached a trial.» In law, what does dismissed mean? | *Ended the court case without a trial | Moved the case to a bigger court | Asked the jury to decide the case | Made the case longer for the lawyers
